diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Quick_Get_Started_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Quick_Get_Started_Guide.md
index fb33cb368..15478985e 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Quick_Get_Started_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Quick_Get_Started_Guide.md
@@ -212,6 +212,7 @@ For the new content or modified one in this mod (AdvCiv-SAS), only English trans
 - tweaked and enhanced old razing logic so we that we (i.e. AI (excluding the barbarian player itself, but as for cities applies more or less to all cities even non-barbarian ones if i'm not mistaken anyways et) players but anyways etc) now raze cities in the early (as of now first 120 turns adjusted to game speed anyways etc) game if they are not close enough to make it worth the early investment. This helps not spread our military forces (which was a major issue in base advciv when it happened, often with most troops being in the new captured faraway city while core ones would be less defended, hopefully much saner and stronger razing now if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc) and scrace economy ressources (city maintenance would be increased per city, pop is generally low in these cities plus the time to build improvements or/and culture or such there, plus the city maintenance in the city itself, etc) so that they stay focused. Indirectly, it may often lead to less fog busting so more barbarians, which is good since it's far from us so will weaken our rivals if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc. As a result of this, AI should be much stronger in the early game, and hopefully no longer split in two making it much easier to defeat (especially if most forces are in the new city). See [64 - (Greatly enhanced) AI not razing faraway cities at captures - now we raze them if we are in the early game and they are not close enough, thanks to changes and tweaks in CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc) for details anyways etc.
 - Fixed and enhanced the issue of AI overbuilding units with defender UNITAIs when it has few cities for the current stage of the game (so no need to defend that hard, build attackers to expand rather to save on unit cost and leverage unit count advantage + make up for being boxed in or other causes for having low cities anyways etc) or simply already a majority of units with a defender UNITAI (for example joao ai had 36 longbowmen at turn 130, almost all with UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE but only 3 cities, very very bad and inefficient, causing his downfall due to not devleopping enough and preparing for war instead by having a more versatile UNITAI composition anyways etc), results may have been much better if some of these units were attacker UNITAI units or versatile UNITAI units rather anyways etc. To address this, we now hijack the UnitAI of next units we produce onwards in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` if we are not in danger (`!bDanger` anyways etc) and these criterion are met, i.e. for relevant AI players if i am not mistaken anyways etc, and make them offense or versatile UNITAIs based on luck and if unit is eligible (for example Joao AI had many longbowmen with UNITAI_COUNTER, still defending cities if i'm not mistaken but ready to be used as a roaming or offensive stack maybe if i'm not mistaken anyways etc; or justinian AI had 19 longbowmen, but many in a roaming stack with UNITAI_COUNTER, and both these AIs that had low cities or/and exess longbowmen now have a much better middle game, not collapsing to bigger rivals that were a bit thin, but instead making military gains due to better pre-middle game preparation). Note: active only in the early game as is when most expansion happens and cities are weakest, then later on we don't use this logic anymore to not alter gameplay too much or cause issues, plus cities are defended and handled well enough hopefully by then to not need our management and early correction if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc. See for details [53.2 - (Fixed and enhanced) Joao AI building way too many defenders (36 longbowmen at turn 130!! Almost all with UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE or similar) while being boxed in with only 3 cities, instead of making about half of these offense units or versatile ones to punish overextending thin neighbour, fixed by having an early phase "we have expectedly too few cities at this stage of the game, no need to overbuild anymore denders at this stage of the game, switch to offense or versatile UNITAI rather" and "our military composition has way too many defender UNITAIs, switch to offense or versatile UNITAIs", which seemingly fix the issue anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) anyways etc.
 - Tremendously improved AI overbuilding trebuchets in particular but more generally siege units, especially when it is bad like being weaker (trebuchets are useless and very hammer inefficient if not strictly to attack city tiles, catapults or cannons or such are also not too versatile or/and used correctly by AI to defend for example). Used various conditions in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to try to make siege units production as minimal as possible, up to none at all if needed, but if other conditions are met but anyways etc hopefully not too low (a bit low as of now but much better than before when it was too strong). As a result, AIs should have a more varied offensive stack composition, as well as being better at defense when weaker, as seems the case in autoplay test i ran at a glance but anyways etc. See for details [53.3 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding siege units, in particular trebuchets but not only, where they are detrimental to do build, in particular when weaker but not only anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc).
+- removed `UNITAI_CITY_COUNTER` from non-versatile enough units such as the UNIT_MACEMAN, as they are not versatile enough to be reliable city defenders while still being good offense units (too easy to punish with a stack of knight units that are good against them, even a crossbow stack could defeat defending macemen, so use them for offense rather and disable them from here as well as in similar places anyways etc). They may be good against pikemen, but pikemen don't often attack cities and are not that efficient for that, so prefer macemen to focus more on offense unitai roles if i am not mistaken but anyways etc, and same for other units if any have that issue as well anyways etc.
 
